Kind: widen
Issue: #762
Holds open: both ways the klog forwarder loses bytes, on purpose. char_server is forced into the x86-64 bundle in uros/CMakeLists.txt -- it is off by default, and ablate.sh configures each arm from the reference build's options rather than the preset, so a preset change never reached the arms (the first A/B: 0 of 4, the flood had never run). Before its first read the forwarder floods the ring with 320 numbered lines, about 71 KB against a 64 KiB ring, so the kernel moves its cursor; and the first write after the flood is refused as a tty would refuse it. The flood's last line and the refusal's announcement open run-x86_64.sh's two #762 pairs, closed by the lines saying what was lost -- and the arm's own run-x86_64.sh fails a boot in which the flood never ran, so neither arm can pass for want of it.
Run: --entry 14 1200 -smp 1

diff --git a/scripts/run-x86_64.sh b/scripts/run-x86_64.sh
index 0ac8ea19..53c0ff1a 100755
--- a/scripts/run-x86_64.sh
+++ b/scripts/run-x86_64.sh
@@ -623,6 +623,12 @@ must_report 'taskpanic_load: started' 'taskpanic_load: .*no load' \
 # before the forwarder reads it, and one write refused on purpose -- because
 # no other boot prints either first line.  The flood's last line is the
 # newest in the ring and survives the overrun it causes.
+# 762-widen: the flood must have run, or both arms pass for want of it.
+grep -aq 'klog flood: done' "$LOG" || {
+	echo "  FAILED: 762-widen-klog-loss's flood never ran -- the forwarder is not in this boot"
+	echo "  log: $LOG"
+	exit 1
+}
 must_report 'klog flood: done' 'char_server: the kernel.s log is missing [0-9]* bytes here -- the ring overran' \
 	'The flood ran the ring over before the forwarder read it, and the forwarder said nothing of what it lost (#762).'
 must_report 'klog: the first write after the flood is refused on purpose' 'char_server: the kernel.s log is missing up to [0-9]* bytes here -- the tty refused' \
